# Security-sensitive files require explicit ownership
#
# `SECURITY.md` here named a root file that no longer exists: the security
# policy is `.github/SECURITY.md` since the 2026-10-10 dedup (issue #109 item 1,
# ruling D186), and a root-anchored pattern with no matching path is a rule that
# silently owns nothing. Same for `contractiles/`, which was never a root path in
# this repository — the contractiles have always lived under .machine_readable/,
# which the line above already covers.
.github/SECURITY.md @hyperpolymath
.github/workflows/ @hyperpolymath
.machine_readable/ @hyperpolymath

# Repository shape is owner-level: the allowlist and the gates that read it.
.machine_readable/root-allow.txt @hyperpolymath
scripts/check-root-shape.sh @hyperpolymath
scripts/check-lock-sync.sh @hyperpolymath
scripts/check-doc-links.sh @hyperpolymath

